check_cilium_residue (Rex::Rancher::Uninstall) only offers a reboot. On otho (2026-10-31, ex-cp-lab rke2 agent after rke2-uninstall.sh) the residue came out without a reboot, and the new RKE2+Cilium install then came up cleanly (OCP apply exit 0):

1. rm -rf /sys/fs/bpf/cilium (dropping the pinned links detaches tcx from_netdev/to_netdev on the NICs and the socketlb cgroup links)
2. bpftool cgroup tree / cgroup detach for remaining cil_* programs on /sys/fs/cgroup (the rest of the socket LB)
3. rm /sys/fs/bpf/tc/globals/cilium_*
4. umount /run/cilium/cgroupv2; rm -rf /run/cilium
Verified: `bpftool net` and `bpftool cgroup tree` without cil_, no mount left, SSH stable.

Proposal: an opt-in cleanup (e.g. `clean_cilium_residue => 1` or its own `clean_cilium_residue` method) that does exactly that and afterwards runs the probe again. The default stays die. The die message names the cleanup as an alternative to a reboot. Reason: hosts with other services (otho runs llama-swap, nvidia-persistenced) should not have to be rebooted for this.

Done means: the method is idempotent, the probe comes back clean afterwards, tests for the command line, and the die text mentions the option. Live check only on a released test host.

From kubernetes-ocp (k248 live test). OCP would expose the option later via its own card.

